WEBVTT

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:15.070
It's been a long time since 
a game got me that fired up.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.440
Let's lock horns again sometime.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.250
Hey!

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.180
Boy, Sekizan. You're looking blue.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.250
He's been like this since this morning.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.260
There's nothing wrong with showing your 
emotions when the juniors aren't around.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.160
If we'd played with the same 
determination at the start

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.800
that we showed at the end of the game...

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.860
we... we would've done better!

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.840
Like I said, since this morning.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.540
I see. But he's right.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.420
Komori-san said we'd gotten stronger, 
but a loss is still a loss.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.400
We're weak.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.720
We need to get stronger.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:10.410
It was that moment! That scrum!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.630
That's enough, Taku.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.340
<b>Rugby Team</b>

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.840
We're going to the beach.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.610
The beach?

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:23.680
Th-That sounds fun.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.630
Seriously? I don't have any swim trunks.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.350
You can wear your shorts.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.860
Practice starts in an hour.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:36.310
It's about six kilometers to the coast at 
Arukimizu, the closest beach to Jinko.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:40.240
I'm heading there now. 
You'll be running there.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.060
What?

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.930
Get moving.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.030
We're running there? What?

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.500
Six... kilometers?

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.320
What?!

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:36.040
<b>Episode 10
 I Ate Too Much Shaved Ice</b>

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.980
It's been 40 minutes so far.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.420
Oh, Ebumi's first.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.830
Hey, don't stop moving.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.700
Lactic acid will build up in your muscles.

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.920
Here they come.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.700
The hour has passed. Come on,
Hirota-senpai, you can do it.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.220
Dammit...

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.470
Okay, pair up and do wheelbarrows.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.900
Do ten 50-meter laps.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:11.430
Seriously? That's what we always do.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.460
Well, whatever. It's nice out here.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.560
Begin.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.440
All right!

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.840
I-It's so hard to walk!

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.990
And it's hot! The sand's so hot!

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.110
No lollygagging.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.560
Hey, how much longer are 
you going to sit there?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.280
Don't make light of a fatty's troubles.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.010
Shut it. Hurry it up.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.880
W-We're finished!

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:51.960
Okay, now carry each other for 20 laps.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.280
What?

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.020
Begin.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.610
Just how heavy are you?

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.400
Gion!

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.160
Not bad.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.950
This is nothing.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:20.570
Ow!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.460
You dumb crab! Die!

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.600
Not bad.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:27.220
This is... nothing.

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.220
Y-You're heavy.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:34.740
Sekizan, could you stop clasping 
your hands together like that?

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:36.730
What?

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:41.400
Excuse me. Will someone pair up with me?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.900
I will.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.910
No, thank you.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:01.990
Okay, everyone's finished. 
Time for the next exercise.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.670
Manager.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.920
Yes, sir.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:10.290
Shovels?

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:11.550
Dig holes.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.180
Digging holes uses all 
the muscles in your body.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:20.190
Standing your ground trains 
your body's reactions, too.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:24.630
Our school doesn't have any weights.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.440
But beaches are free.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.110
What?

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.700
Get started.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.380
This is hard.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.710
Heave-ho!

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.960
This has nothing to do with rugby.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:49.840
What's wrong with it?

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.020
I've never dug a hole before.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:55.850
I bet it'll build muscles 
I've never worked before.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:07:00.340
We'll be able to do things 
we couldn't do before.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.360
Sekizan's really getting into it.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.880
Fill them back in once 
you've finished digging.

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.840
What?!

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.060
What?

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:31.030
We've finished filling them in!

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.010
Okay, that's enough.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:42.040
Front row. Gather round.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:44.480
Sumo wrestle here.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.240
S-Sumo?

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.280
Oh, right. The May Honbasho 
tournament just ended.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.420
It's not like I'm dying to 
watch sumo wrestling.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.530
Hurry it up.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.530
Ready... fight!

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.550
That was always gonna happen.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.930
What's going on?

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:13.340
No one can beat Hirota 
in a head-to-head.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:14.730
Again.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:15.440
What?

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:18.100
This is rough.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.680
Ready...

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:22.100
That's it. That posture.

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:23.340
Huh?

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:25.050
That's the ruck posture.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:29.230
The lower player wins in a ruck.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.740
Start from that position and...

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:32.490
Fight!

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:38.240
Push your opponent up 
diagonally and flip him over.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:40.660
All right!

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:45.910
That's it. The sand is soft,
so it doesn't hurt.

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:48.590
You can improve your balance, too.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:51.170
Start sumo wrestling.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:54.190
That looks fun. Let me join you.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:55.300
Hirota, fight me.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:00.310
All right. I'll take you on.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:02.090
Ready...

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:04.560
If I win, you'd better buy me
some fried chicken.

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.300
<i>I just remembered!</i>

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:11.330
<i>He ate the fried chicken 
in my lunch the other day!</i>

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:12.820
Fight!

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.310
Take this!

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:16.450
Take this and this and this!

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.580
This is what you get for eating my food!

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:21.950
Did they...

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:22.890
...disappear?

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.460
We forgot to fill in a hole over there!

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:29.080
Hey, are you guys okay?

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.900
Hey, Raita! Where are you?

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:36.170
Someone get a shovel!

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.090
That was rough.

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.190
I'm dying.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:43.180
Are you okay?

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:44.810
I'm dead.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:51.570
There are 147 days until the preliminaries.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:57.570
If we practice two hours every day,
that's 294 hours.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:01.790
That's less than thirteen days.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:06.360
It's up to you how you spend them.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.850
Th-Thirteen days?

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:11.770
What? That can't be good.

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:13.510
At this rate, we'll be screwed.

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:14.500
Captain!

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.760
No, we can double it.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:20.640
Starting tomorrow, we'd like to 
conduct morning practices here.

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:27.770
Sure. Prepare yourselves for it.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:35.890
S-Sekizan, you bastard.
You shouldn't have said that.

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:39.150
Dammit. Well, I'm going 
to have fun while I can.

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:41.160
The beach!

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:43.540
Hey, what about your clothes?

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:45.860
Just leave them there.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:47.160
It's cold.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:54.330
I want to try playing 
the number eight role.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.210
Or do you think it's too hard?

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:59.380
I'd like to try a back position.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.650
It's pretty hard.

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:03.930
There are a lot of amazing backs.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.680
Mikami, you'll play prop, right?

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.550
Because of how I look?

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.090
Yeah, exactly.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:14.180
I hope we're assigned positions soon
so we can play in a game.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:32.210
Hey, I want to talk to you.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:43.970
<b>Hey!</b>

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:43.970
<b>Someone 
help!</b>

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:52.910
Why are you sitting there? Go away.

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:59.840
The first-years were talking about 
which positions they wanted to play.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:03.710
I have a question for you.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:06.560
Do you think I'd make a good winger?

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:09.240
Or would a different position
suit me better?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.460
How did you decide?

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:15.260
I dunno.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.530
Before I knew it, I was playing fly-half.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.970
Probably because I was the best player
at the rugby school.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:30.920
Dammit. If only I were
as big as my brother...

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.180
He's at least as tall as the captain.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.360
You have a brother?

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.360
Yeah. You, too?

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:42.230
A younger one.

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:46.850
He's the one who invited me
to join the rugby school.

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:50.120
Really? Your brother plays rugby, too?

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:58.760
My brother should play, too.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:00.580
He's big enough.

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:07.610
I'm small. And I still can't pass
or catch the ball properly.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:12.520
You're lucky. You can do everything.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:16.900
<i>You're lucky. You can do everything.</i>

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.510
<i>You're lucky. You can do everything.</i>

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:28.410
The best player on the team plays fly-half.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.910
Really? It's just a coincidence.

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:33.540
Oharano. Oharano.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.410
Come here.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:36.780
He's calling you.

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:40.510
Uh, he could be talking about you. Let's go.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:42.670
Nah.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:49.480
When the coach asks for Oharano, 
he's always talking about you.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.690
Gion-kun, do you like rugby?

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:20.630
I hate it.

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.680
I'm actually...

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:31.600
...not sure anymore.

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:40.050
After all, I can't do anything.

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:44.670
I didn't get to play in the game
the other day, either.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:46.750
Nothing fun has happened yet.

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:49.700
You're still digging? You're an idiot.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.910
Shut up.

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:55.680
What was that for?!

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:59.660
You're an idiot, too. 
Why do you play if you hate it?

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:03.690
Shut up!

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.410
Shut up!

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:07.340
Timeout! Timeout!

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:09.220
My brother...

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:10.720
Huh?

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:15.470
Until my brother starts playing 
rugby again, I won't quit!

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:24.660
He loved rugby way more than I ever did.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:30.740
He never complained like you did.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.050
Not once.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:38.410
For years,

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:43.000
he patiently endured everything!

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:47.960
Unlike you, he didn't complain
just because he couldn't do something!

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.720
I was lying, idiot!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:56.340
It doesn't matter if I'm facing
hotshots like you

00:15:56.340 --> 00:15:58.600
or giants like Iwashimizu...

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:01.100
I'll knock you all down.

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:05.860
I'll show you that I'm the strongest one of all!

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:09.860
That's impossible, idiot.

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:12.390
Shut up! I can do it, idiot!

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:14.900
You can't, idiot!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:16.870
I can, idiot!

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:18.340
You can't!

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:19.450
I can!

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.600
You can't!

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.230
I can!

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:23.930
There's no way you can!

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:26.550
I can! Why can't I?

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:27.810
Hey, stop that!

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.890
You asshole, you can't!

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.600
I can't lift my arms anymore.

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:54.670
This kind of practice is 
probably right for you.

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:57.700
You'll get better at tackling.

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:04.410
I still don't really get rugby,
but I like tackling.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.940
You'd probably make a good flanker.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:12.170
If you want to knock down
 the big lunkheads, I mean.

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:17.180
Cocky guys like you make good forwards.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.560
If you're trying to be smart, that is.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:32.000
Which one's the flanker?

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.940
Rugby's not for you, Gion-kun.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:37.700
Give me a minute. I'll remember.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:41.170
They're gone.

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.450
You guys are idiots.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:49.060
You want to be a flanker?

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:50.750
You?

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:55.470
Yeah, but I'm not sure what 
you're meant to do in that position.

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:58.010
Do you think someone will teach me?

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:02.250
You playing flanker? 
That might not be a bad idea.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:06.270
Oh, right. We don't have 
practice this Sunday.

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:09.610
Okay! I've got an idea, Gion.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:11.110
Huh?

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:15.180
Let's go spy on the champions of Kanagawa.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:27.890
<b>Ryoin Academy</b>

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.320
I can't read that.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.880
"Ryoin Academy."

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:23.960
They've made it to Nationals 
fifteen years in a row.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:28.250
Ryoin is the strongest team in Kanagawa.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.000
Excuse the intrusion.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.360
And we're third-year middle schoolers,
 here to look around the school.

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:36.760
Will anyone believe that story?

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:39.700
Rather than explaining 
to you what a flanker does,

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:44.200
you should watch Kanagawa's 
best flanker in action.

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:48.510
Today, they're playing Kanto Academy.

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:50.910
They made the Kanagawa quarters last year.

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:53.020
It should be a pretty good game.

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.770
Really?

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:57.900
To put it in Old Man Komo's words...

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:58.900
"Steal it."

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.410
Steal what?

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:03.310
Oh, um... their techniques, I guess?

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:08.410
Oh, dang. Sounds like 
they've already started.

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:11.110
You can do it, boys!

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:12.720
Sekito-kun!

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.290
Let's watch from over there, Gion-kun.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:20.930
Y-Yeah...

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.970
This should be a good enough spot.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.740
Let's see. Their flanker is...

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:30.050
Look for #6 and #7 on the blue team.

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:30.980
Sure.

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:36.630
What a tackle.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:40.360
#7. That's him.

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:42.360
He's huge.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:46.120
That's the best flanker in Kanagawa?

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:48.650
You'd think so, wouldn't you?

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:49.380
Huh?

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:55.890
No matter how big or good at tackling 
you are, it doesn't matter if you miss!

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:02.590
That was low.

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:05.470
Thanks for the ball.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:06.470
Kokuto.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:10.060
#6.

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:13.560
Damn it! Get that ball back!

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:15.450
Sekito!

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:15.980
Oui...

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.820
Surround him! W-We'll crush him!

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:29.740
He dove through their legs?

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:43.050
That's the 165 centimeter tall 
number one flanker in Kanagawa...

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.240
Kirishima Sekito.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:46.550
Nice pass!

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:47.500
Nice try.

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:51.720
And the muscly #7 is his twin brother,
Kirishima Kokuto.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:01.190
Damn. His tackles...

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:06.160
No, all of his movements were so amazing, 
even I could see how good they were.

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:09.560
Even among the huge forwards on Ryoin,

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:14.500
Kirishima Sekito has secured a regular 
spot with his low form and his speed.

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:19.510
Wow...

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:26.360
Watch closely, Gion.

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:27.290
Yeah.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:34.270
<b>Ryoin</b>

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:38.140
Wow, that was unbelievably fast!

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:40.040
I know, right?

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.270
What are you doing?

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:44.300
What? Spying on them, of course.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:46.030
Huh?

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:48.530
Think you'll learn anything?

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:55.480
You're huge! Who the hell are you?

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.790
<b>Ryoin</b>

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:58.790
Huh? A Ryoin jersey?

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:01.980
What are you doing here?

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:05.790
I was late.

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:12.560
I ate too much shaved ice and 
gave myself a stomachache.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next Time: "You Have No Feel For the Game"</b>

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:48.790
Next time: "You Have No Feel For the Game."
